<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Jan-April oil revenue at $515.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Jan-April oil revenue at $515.5 mln.</headline>
<text>
<p>BOGOTA, May 9 Reuter - Colombia's oil export revenues for January-April totalled $515.5 million, the state oil company Ecopetrol said in a statement Friday.</p>
<p>The statement did not give a detailed breakdown for the four-month period. But it said oil exports totalled 8.6 million barrels in April, a month when export earnings totalled more than $148 million.</p>
<p>In other developments, Ecopetrol said 78,000 barrels of crude oil had been spilled in 24 rebel sabotage attacks on the Cano Limon-Covenas oil pipeline so far this year.</p>
<p>The pipleline has been dynamited 460 times since it opened in 1986 in attacks that spilled 1.5 million barrels of crude.</p>
<p>(-- Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944)</p>
